/mvnw text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# Everything the container build and the server read is read by Linux tools, so it is
# stored and checked out with LF whatever core.autocrlf says on a Windows machine. A CRLF
# shell script fails on Linux with "bash\r: No such file or directory", and a CRLF
# Dockerfile or Caddyfile is at best confusing to diff.
/Dockerfile text eol=lf
/.dockerignore text eol=lf
/deploy/** text eol=lf
